  "name": "Graded Pragmatic Belief Allocation Across Competitor Structures",
  "summary": "Listeners distribute 10 confidence points across candidate referents on utterance and prior trials, directly measuring the full graded posterior distribution over objects.",
  "charter": {
    "question": "When listeners report their full graded belief distribution over candidate referents rather than a single winner-take-all choice, do their secondary and tertiary probability assignments follow recursive pragmatic inference, competitor confusion avoidance, or a binary singleton heuristic?"
